.TH pepe-completions 1  pepe "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pepe\-completions \- Tab completion for your shell: print the script, or \-\-install it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe completions\fR [\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISHELL\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tab completion for your shell: print the script, or \-\-install it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
Put the script and the man pages in place and add the line the shell\*(Aqs startup file needs, so tab completion works in the next shell
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
With \-\-install: say what would be done, and do nothing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISHELL\fR]
bash, zsh, fish or powershell; the current shell when left out
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.RE
